# No institute hardcode

## Rule

Shared code does not name a tenant. Tenant identity is data. The data lives in the theme document, the brand layer, and `site_settings`.

Client-only code lives in `src/variants/owned/<slug>/`. The variant declares `owner`. A file in that folder may name its own slug. It must not name another slug.

Behavior that changes per tenant uses a domain setting. Use a domain name such as `register.extras_pack = family_guide`. Do not branch on a slug.

Copy for one client lives in that tenant's document. Do not add a tenant namespace to the shared dictionaries.

SQL brand data starts with `-- ge:brand-data <slug>`. `isBrandDataMigration` reads that line. A slug in the file name does not mark the file.

## Guard

`npm run check:institute-hardcode` scans `src/**/*.{ts,tsx,css,json}`.

| Code | What it finds |
|---|---|
| `slug_comparison` | A slug compared with `===`, `!==`, or `case` |
| `slug_table` | A slug used as an object key or array item |
| `slug_file_name` | A slug in a file name |
| `slug_css` | A slug in a CSS class or variable |
| `slug_dictionary` | A slug key in a dictionary file |

Allowed paths: `src/variants/owned/<slug>/**` for that slug, `src/__tests__/**`, `e2e/**`, `docs/**`, `supabase/**`, `scripts/**`, `public/**`.

The baseline is `scripts/institute-hardcode-baseline.json`. Do not raise a count. Do not add a path to the allow list without a spec. `--update-baseline` only lowers counts.

```ts
// Bad. A new tenant needs a new branch.
if (kind === "nago") return <NagoLanding />;

// Good. The document picks the variant. The code does not name the tenant.
return <SectionView variantId={section.variantId} />;
```
